# The scheduler descriptor (design 0025 §4.1, D7, D17). Its PRESENCE is how the
# control plane knows Volcano runs here: the BatchJob composition renders the
# Volcano path and the Team composition composes the leaf queues only while this
# ConfigMap exists (together with the Queue CRD), and `adhar batch queues` and the
# Console read it. It ships with core/volcano, so it exists exactly where Volcano
# is synced; to move every BatchJob back to the native path, remove it first
# (README, A2.10).
#
#   scheduler           the scheduler the compositions hand pods to
#   version             the pinned Volcano release (TestVolcanoPinsOneVersionEverywhere)
#   gang                "true": partitioned jobs run as an all-or-nothing gang
#   rootQueue           the parent of every team leaf (root-queue.yaml.tmpl)
#   prodDeservedCPU/    every team's prod leaf deserved share, what lets prod reclaim
#   prodDeservedMemory  from dev and test. By default the larger of 4500m / 7Gi (the
#                       design's largest example gang) and a quarter of the ceiling,
#                       at most the ceiling (D17); rendered at seed time from the
#                       cluster like the root queue. A platform created before the
#                       seed carried them renders the reference values below.
#
# Read-only for everyone but Argo CD: the Team composition trusts these numbers.
# Wave 2, with the root queue it names.
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: adhar-batch-scheduler
  namespace: adhar-system
  annotations:
    argocd.argoproj.io/sync-wave: "2"
  labels:
    app.kubernetes.io/name: volcano
    app.kubernetes.io/component: batch-scheduler-descriptor
    app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: adhar
data:
  scheduler: volcano
  version: v1.16.0
  gang: "true"
  rootQueue: adhar-batch
  prodDeservedCPU: '{{ or .BatchProdDeservedCPU "5500m" }}'
  prodDeservedMemory: '{{ or .BatchProdDeservedMemory "7Gi" }}'
